timestamp=2026-11-09T09:12:09.850Z level=INFO run=e6571189 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# Look at the bad employee mappings again\n# 84731091580 in timesheet vs 87031491580 in employees (Agnieszka Zając) - close\n# 62020111425 vs 65020111422 (Magdalena Wójcik) - different birth year digit\n# 16102016795 vs 96102016751 (Tomasz Wójcik) - 1 vs 9 at start, 95 vs 51 at end?\n# 68011910138 vs 68011810139 (Tomasz Kurek) - 9 vs 8 in month/day part? 680119 vs 680118 (month 01 vs 01, day 19 vs 18), last digits 0138 vs 0139\n# 15720759071 - not obvious match. Let us look up in timesheet what name would make sense? Or see if it matches any employee by other fields?\n# But we only have PESEL to match employees. Maybe look at facility_id, position patterns? Or see common typos\n# Also compare full numbers: 75020759171 (Jan Król) vs 15720759071 - swapped prefix? 75 vs 15, ends 9171 vs 9071 - close but not exact\n# Another: 62020111425 (bad) vs 65020111422 (good) - 62 vs 65, ends 425 vs 422\n# Could be OCR/typo. The task says: \"If any invalid or inconsistent data are found in the input, they should be corrected where possible based on available data, or otherwise excluded from the final results.\"\n# So try to correct by fuzzy matching to known employees\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
