timestamp=2026-11-09T09:12:43.032Z level=INFO run=e6571189 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# Now look at how to handle invalid/inconsistent data as per task\n# The task says: \"If any invalid or inconsistent data are found in the input,\n# they should be corrected where possible based on available data, or otherwise excluded from the final results.\"\n# Invalid/inconsistent could include:\n# - Bad dates (e.g., 2025-06-31) - can correct to valid date (maybe last day of month, or 30th)\n# - Bad performed_tasks format - can parse by fixing brackets/splitting\n# - Invalid task IDs in performed_tasks (e.g., 244 not in tasks.csv) - maybe exclude those task IDs from bonus calculation? Or treat row as problematic?\n# - Invalid employee_id (not in employees.csv) - if we can correct by fuzzy matching, do that. If not, exclude the row?\n# - Missing or weird hours? hours_worked looks ok numerically\n# Also \"any bonuses earned for completed tasks in that month\" - so bonus is per completed task as defined in tasks.csv? Yes, each task gives pay_per_completion when performed.\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
