timestamp=2026-11-09T09:12:57.469Z level=INFO run=e6571189 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# Let us look at task 590 (Weekend and holiday work, pay 160, medium, OUT_OF_STANDARD)\n# And row 203: if employee were 87031491580 (Agnieszka Zając), her hourly_rate is 27.0, hours 2, bonus 160 -> total 214. The salary_amount in file was 567 - but we compute ourselves. So for our calculation, the employee identity matters for hourly rate.\n# Similarly for row 793: employee 62020111425 maps to 65020111422 (Magdalena Zofia Wójcik, F, born 1965-02-01, hourly_rate 27.0). hours 5, tasks [123, 900] - task 123 is \"Cleanup after flooding\", pay_per_completion 290; task 900 is \"Urgent on-call jobs\", pay 160 (from tasks.csv: task 900 pay_per_completion 160, category OUT_OF_STANDARD, medium). So bonus = 290+160=450. Total = 5*27 + 450 = 135+450=585. So corrected employee makes sense.\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
