timestamp=2026-11-09T09:13:54.001Z level=INFO run=e6571189 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta\nimport csv\n\n# Find the Tuesday that starts the cycle - earliest record's date is 2025-03-04 which is Tuesday\nstart = datetime(2025, 3, 4)  # Tuesday\n# Generate billing periods? Are they monthly periods starting on Tuesdays?\n# If billing period is monthly and starts on Tuesday, then each period is from Tuesday of that period to Tuesday of next period minus 1 day? Or just month-long aligned to that start.\n# Or maybe the \"billing month\" is defined such that the first billing day of the month is the Tuesday of that calendar month (or the first Tuesday of the month, or the Tuesday that falls on/after some boundary)?\n# Alternatively, look at the dates: earliest is 2025-03-04 (Tue). All data is in March–June 2025. Maybe the billing month is the calendar month, and the \"starts on Tuesday\" is just saying when payment happens (e.g., paid on the Tuesday of that month) - not affecting calculation. That’s plausible. Then we just bucket by calendar month (year, month).\n# That’s the most straightforward. Let us also check the sample of how others might interpret - but we have to infer. Another interpretation: billing periods are 4-week periods starting on Tue? That doesn’t give \"monthly\" in calendar terms. Or periods are aligned such that each billing period starts on Tue and lasts until next Tue? Then periods are weekly. But task says \"monthly salary\".\n# Another reading: \"For each month, the billing period...\" - so within each month, the billing period starts on that weekday (Tue). So the billing period in March starts on the first Tuesday of March that is the \"inherited\" start? Or the Tuesday of that month that corresponds to the pattern. Since earliest record is on a Tuesday (2025-03-04), and 2025-03-04 is in March, maybe for each month M, the billing period starts on the Tuesday of month M that is the same relative Tuesday? Or simply bucket by calendar month, and the Tuesday note is just operational detail. That’s more plausible for the calculation requested.\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
