timestamp=2026-11-09T09:14:15.911Z level=INFO run=e6571189 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta\n\n# Build Tuesday-starting billing periods of ~4 weeks? Or month-long aligned to Tue start anchored at earliest Tue\nstart = datetime(2025, 3, 4)  # Tue\n# Generate periods\nperiods = []\n# Generate for range covering data\ncur = start\nfor i in range(10):\n    end = cur + timedelta(days=28) - timedelta(days=1)  # 4 weeks minus 1 day? Or just use 28-day blocks\n    periods.append((i, cur, end))\n    cur = cur + timedelta(days=28)\n    if cur > datetime(2025, 12, 31):\n        break\n\nfor p in periods[:5]:\n    print(p[0], p[1].strftime('%Y-%m-%d'), 'to', p[2].strftime('%Y-%m-%d'))\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
