timestamp=2026-11-09T09:14:23.290Z level=INFO run=e6571189 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# Compare to calendar months in data: data goes up to 2025-06-30 (latest). If periods are 28-day blocks anchored to 2025-03-04 Tue, then period 0 ends 2025-03-31, period 1 is 2025-04-01 to 2025-04-28, period 2 2025-04-29 to 2025-05-26, period 3 2025-05-27 to 2025-06-23, period 4 2025-06-24 onward. So entries from 2025-06-24 to 2025-06-30 would fall in period 4 (July-ish billing period conceptually). Also 2025-06-30 is in period 4 (ends 2025-07-21, so 2025-06-30 is within). But how does this map to \"monthly salary for each month\" as required?\n# Or alternatively, billing periods might be calendar-month-based but starting on the Tuesday of that month? For example, March billing period starts on Tue 2025-03-04 (the first Tue in March or that specific Tue). Then ends on Mon 2025-04-01 (day before next Tue)? That’s not quite a month.\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
